  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nA shortwave trough is expected to arrive from the northwest on \nMonday, effectively squashing the upper ridge toward the \nsoutheast. Enhanced lift with continued moisture will increase \nshower and thunderstorm chances late Monday through Tuesday \nacross the southwest/central Idaho terrain. Further cooling can \nbe expected Tuesday as the trough makes its way east through \nthe Northern Rockies. The resultant west-northwest flow aloft \nwill then nudge the moisture out of the forecast area while \nalso promoting slightly cooler than normal temperatures late \nTuesday through Wednesday. Thereafter, latest model runs are \ndepicting the return of the upper level ridge across the West \nby late in the week, which would promote warming and potentially\nre-open the door for the next round of moisture.",
